diff --git a/docs/source/argument_files.rst b/docs/source/argument_files.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5e91933
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/source/argument_files.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+.. _Argument Files:
+
+==============
+Argument Files
+==============
+
+Cyclopts can expand arguments from files, similar to :mod:`argparse`'s
+``fromfile_prefix_chars``, GCC's ``@file``, and Java's ``@argfile``.
+Enable the feature by specifying one or more prefix characters:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+   from cyclopts import App
+
+   app = App(fromfile_prefix_chars="@")
+
+
+   @app.command
+   def run(*, workers: int = 1):
+       print(f"Running with {workers} workers.")
+
+
+   app()
+
+A token beginning with a configured prefix character is replaced, in place, by
+the arguments read from the file named after the prefix. For example, the
+following file:
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+   run
+   --workers
+   16
+
+can be used from the command line as:
+
+.. code-block:: console
+
+   $ my-script @run.args
+   Running with 16 workers.
+
+By default, each line of the file is treated as exactly one argument. Argument
+files may reference other argument files, and those references are expanded
+recursively. Lines are read using UTF-8 encoding.
+
+Custom line conversion
+----------------------
+Pass a ``convert_arg_line_to_args`` callable to split lines or otherwise
+transform them before parsing. The callable receives one line and must return
+an iterable of argument strings.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+   import shlex
+
+   app = App(
+       fromfile_prefix_chars="@",
+       convert_arg_line_to_args=shlex.split,
+   )
+
+You can also assign a converter after construction, or override the
+:meth:`App.convert_arg_line_to_args` method in an :class:`App` subclass. The
+default implementation is equivalent to:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+   def convert_arg_line_to_args(line: str) -> list[str]:
+       return [line]
